# What the image build does not need to see.
#
# The build stage is `COPY . .`, so everything here is sent to the daemon
# before a single layer is built. web/node_modules alone is 156MB of files
# the Go stage cannot use — the UI stage installs its own from
# package-lock.json — and .git is another 17MB of history.
#
# bin/ and internal/webui/dist are the sharper ones: they are *build output*,
# so sending a local build into the image risks a stale UI landing in a layer
# before the in-image build writes the real one.

.git
.github
.gstack
.claude
.cursor

web/node_modules
web/dist
node_modules

bin
internal/webui/dist

context
docs
npm
*.md

.goreleaser.yaml
.dockerignore
Makefile
compose.yaml
.devcontainer
